			"notes": "**LayBalt QOL** is a free, open-source Hypixel SkyBlock mod for **Minecraft 26.2 on Fabric**. It is built on the [NoammAddons](https://github.com/Noamm9/NoammAddons) core and adds features from [Odin](https://github.com/odtheking/Odin) and OdinClient. Altogether it has more than 180 features, all in one menu. This is LayBalt QOL's first Fabric release on GitHub.\n\n## What's in it\n\n- **Dungeons:** dungeon map with room prediction, secret waypoints, puzzle solvers (Water Board, Blaze, Boulder, Ice Fill and more), Score Calculator, Leap Menu, Star Mob ESP.\n- **Floor 7:** terminal solvers, Auto Terminal with Auto Melody (beta), a terminal simulator (`/lbq termsim`), relic and tick timers.\n- **Fishing:** Auto Fishing and Auto Mob Killer (beta). Record yourself fishing with the Fishing Recorder, and they copy your timing and aim.\n- **Experiments:** Auto Enchanting plays Chronomatron and Ultrasequencer and stops at the max Superpairs clicks of the stake you pick.\n- **Party:** Party Finder Auto Kick by PB, secrets and Magical Power, Party HUD, party chat commands.\n- **And more:** Kuudra helpers, HUDs and render tweaks, storage overlay, item prices, loadout and wardrobe keybinds.\n\nThe full feature list and every command are in the [README](https://github.com/LayBalt/LayBalt-QOL#readme). The changelog since 3.2.0 is in [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/LayBalt/LayBalt-QOL/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Some features automate gameplay, which Hypixel's rules forbid. Use them at your own risk.\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Install [Fabric Loader](https://fabricmc.net/use/) 0.19.3 or newer for Minecraft 26.2. The game needs Java 25. The official launcher brings it; other launchers may need you to select it.\n2. Put these mods in your `mods` folder:\n   - [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api)\n   - [Fabric Language Kotlin](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-language-kotlin) 1.13.13+kotlin.2.4.10 or newer\n   - `LayBaltQOL-3.7.1-26.2.jar` from the assets below\n   - Optional: [Mod Menu](https://modrinth.com/mod/modmenu)\n3. Start Minecraft with the Fabric Loader profile and type `/lbq` in chat to open the menu.\n\nIf you used NoammAddons, Odin or OdinClient, your settings are imported on the first launch. Every imported or skipped setting is listed in `config/LayBaltQOL/import-report.txt`.\n\n## Already on 3.7.0?\n\n3.7.1 makes these changes:\n- Auto Enchanting stops at the max Superpairs clicks of the stake you pick.\n- Party Finder Auto Kick and join stats now work. In 3.7.0 every lookup failed.\n- The dungeon map's run summary shows your teammates' secrets again.\n\n## Privacy\n\nSeveral features send the Minecraft UUIDs of the players they look up to the stats server set in Secrets Counter > API URL, which is Odin's public server by default:\n- Auto Kick\n- join stats\n- the Party Finder tooltip stats\n- `/pfs` and `/lbq cata`\n- Secrets Counter\n- the Dungeon Map's Player Clear Info\n\nNames are first turned into UUIDs by mowojang.matdoes.dev or Mojang. Clear the API URL and none of these lookups are sent. Separately, `/lbq soopy` sends the player name you give it, or your own name if you give none, to soopy.dev.\n\n## Licence\n\nLayBalt QOL's own code is released into the public domain under the Unlicense. It also contains:\n- code from NoammAddons (CC0-1.0), from Odin, OdinClient, dtMap and Nebulune (BSD-3-Clause), from Open-Imaging (Apache-2.0) and from ikumen's today-i-learned (MIT);\n- the AOTV landing prediction, which came in with NoammAddons and is credited there to \"Shizo\", whose licence is unknown;\n- data from SkyHanni-REPO (MIT), and the names and coordinates of Trevor Helper's six mob areas from SkyHanni (LGPL-2.1), which came in with NoammAddons;\n- the Inter font (SIL OFL 1.1);\n- libraries under their own licences.\n\n`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` lists each of them with its licence and includes the licence texts. It is attached below, and the jar carries it as `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES_LayBaltQOL.md`.\n\n\n..."
		}
